Parent: TRA-2873. This is the **cost-basis axis only** ($23.00 of the $44.00 Gain/Loss gap). The mark axis is filed separately so this one is not held up by a design call.

## The defect

`packages/server/src/options-account.ts`, the `for (const incoming of positions)` merge loop in `reconcileTradierPositions`:

```js
if (existing) {
  if (!existing.importedFromTradier) {
    // Engine-opened position covers this OCC symbol - skip so we
    // don't conflict with the engine's own bookkeeping.
    continue;                                    // <-- TRA-2873
  }
  ...
  existing.premiumPaid = incoming.premiumPaid;   // broker truth
```

`TradierOpenOptionPosition.premiumPaid` is already derived from the broker's authoritative `cost_basis` (`packages/engine/src/tradier/options-client.ts`: `cost_basis / quantity / 100`). An **imported** row gets restated to it. An **engine-opened** row takes the `continue` and keeps `premiumPaid = signal.mark` - the scanner's pre-trade NBBO mid - for the life of the position.

